<title>USA: Meredith to take gain from cable sale.</title>
<headline>Meredith to take gain from cable sale.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES, Iowa 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Meredith Corp, through its cable venture with New Heritage Associates, said Friday it completed the sale of its interest in a Twin Cities cable system and expects to record a gain of about $28 million.</p>
<p>The system was sold to a subsidiary of Continental Cablevision Inc.</p>
<p>Total value of the system was placed at $262.5 million. Meredith receives about $125 million in cash from the sale. Continental also will pay about $85 million in Meredith/New Heritage debt.</p>
<p>Meredith is a multimedia company.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
